{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0bf96c9f545e21013613668df7059b1be652419401bc2439d188c07d4db841d2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Verification notes are agent-reported and validated for structure, identity, scope, idempotency, and progress rules, but the server does not independently prove source code or deployments passed."},{"claim_ids":["clm_0e614fceb948b9c17a8db38686ffd89d1975719960b9002ebb55fff992091592"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The released MCP surface contains exactly two tools: project_os_get_context for scoped context reads and project_os_append_progress for validated, idempotent progress appends."},{"claim_ids":["clm_10ff73852c2d3d163a52758640ad407003784c72df654bb915656190d8a43136"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The open-source design keeps private infrastructure behind replaceable adapter boundaries for Git, AI provider, knowledge base, and deployment/reverse proxy, with local JSON persistence for simple evaluation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3d9f3f90adfad3d749fcc33d51447b9f783542095e435499bc12986616b5c9db"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"An Agent API endpoint accepts progress events via POST with X-Project-Key and Idempotency-Key headers, including verification notes, progress percentage, and next step."},{"claim_ids":["clm_505d5baa55fb3ede538bd2052b62e1e06fd6fb18d838d148cb4a6cf6ae650743"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Version 0.3.0 adds a fail-closed first-run contract: the MCP process verifies credential, project binding, scopes, and the exact two-tool surface before Codex uses it, with a project-level config allowlisting only released tools."},{"claim_ids":["clm_82308b18879b1cb426a3bb84259dfdebd0e9dc5a54e8009b41466598cf90cd2e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The stack is React, Vite, TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS on the frontend with Node.js and Express on the backend, persisting to local JSON files by default under an Apache-2.0 license."},{"claim_ids":["clm_875b5289194917f8ebaa709322274ff9972ab45318e387a1a2d1f5436d3cdc14"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The server creates a local Git-backed project record for kickoff, progress, issues, and handoff files, with important progress linked to Git commits as the durable record."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9af94a8357694dc42a69c58861d1d1e0fd2701f6da0d837477594db662c1fa36"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"AI credentials are short-lived (24 hours or 7 days), revocable independently, stored only as hashes, and cannot access members, keys, deletion, publication, or deployment."},{"claim_ids":["clm_bdb1c7199cce60d79e28e986dc1158d3715f255a802840c364e77a0a05701a67"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product does not run Codex, monitor sessions automatically, control a Codex account, or modify an existing source repository; its Git commits belong to the local Project OS record repository."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d5ee7eba328c2168569c7a435e4c6b2e8c81109864dc019699b222a873cbe029"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"High-risk actions such as payment, deletion, role changes, publication, deployment, and rollback stay outside the MCP surface and require explicit human confirmation."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0bf96c9f545e21013613668df7059b1be652419401bc2439d188c07d4db841d2","clm_0e614fceb948b9c17a8db38686ffd89d1975719960b9002ebb55fff992091592","clm_10ff73852c2d3d163a52758640ad407003784c72df654bb915656190d8a43136","clm_3d9f3f90adfad3d749fcc33d51447b9f783542095e435499bc12986616b5c9db","clm_505d5baa55fb3ede538bd2052b62e1e06fd6fb18d838d148cb4a6cf6ae650743","clm_82308b18879b1cb426a3bb84259dfdebd0e9dc5a54e8009b41466598cf90cd2e","clm_875b5289194917f8ebaa709322274ff9972ab45318e387a1a2d1f5436d3cdc14","clm_9af94a8357694dc42a69c58861d1d1e0fd2701f6da0d837477594db662c1fa36","clm_bdb1c7199cce60d79e28e986dc1158d3715f255a802840c364e77a0a05701a67","clm_d5ee7eba328c2168569c7a435e4c6b2e8c81109864dc019699b222a873cbe029"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_c2f7300587ae444b8ff3b0c1c38b5b5f","id":"pg_fdc318f372cf5a1cb680be1991f384dc","maturity":"draft",